// @expect-error 'grow' never finishes being built: each call needs a deeper one. Remove the type argument that refers back to 'grow'.
// @expect-error 'Box' never finishes being built: each call needs a deeper one. Remove the type argument that refers back to 'Box'.
// @expect-error build failed with 2 problems
// @expect-error-at codegen the instantiation-depth guard fires while cloning generic
// bodies; sema never clones them, so this reject belongs to codegen.
// Function-level polymorphic recursion: each call to grow needs a strictly deeper type argument,
// so monomorphization would never terminate. The compiler caps the instantiation cascade and
// reports it rather than expanding until the stack overflows.
class Box<T> {
    T value;
    protected constructor(this.value);
}

grow<T>(T value) -> int {
    return grow<Box<T>>(new Box<T>(value));
}

main() -> int {
    return grow<int>(0);
}
